There is no "yes but" option so I am forced to recommend the game.
Overall it's a good game, don't get me wrong.
BUT you just need to be able to cope with (playing vs AI):
- Having a 90% chance to parry / dogdge and yet being hit more than 50% of the time during the same game, or even 100% of the time in some missions;
- Having your team being ambushed a little too often to my taste, ending up fighting 5 vs 1 and getting destroyed without being able to do anything. In such game, no skills involved when it happens.
- Having your team being spread all over the map when the other one is "conveniently spread" in missions where both teams are supposed to start in random locations;
- Losing all your equipment after having been totally crushed during a mission, because having serious injuries on most of your soldiers is not punishing enough;
Go figure how the RNG works... which can be very frustrating at time. Other than that it's a good game...
